{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-blog-post-js","path":"/010-pop-tops-mark-2/","result":{"data":{"site":{"siteMetadata":{"title":"Wood Times"}},"markdownRemark":{"id":"a33034c0-81c8-57cf-9eb7-c5a4df285c0c","excerpt":"The original pop tops were a hit, but after making a bunch of them I started seeing ways to improve the design. Time for Mark 2.  Starting with fresh oak blanks…","html":"<p>The original pop tops were a hit, but after making a bunch of them I started seeing ways to improve the design. Time for Mark 2.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/493ac/blanks.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Blanks\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/f058b/blanks.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/c26ae/blanks.png 158w,\n/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/6bdcf/blanks.png 315w,\n/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/f058b/blanks.png 630w,\n/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/40601/blanks.png 945w,\n/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/78612/blanks.png 1260w,\n/static/41ca6f13d50e6b30e291fe60a266e2ac/493ac/blanks.png 4032w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>Starting with fresh oak blanks, I refined the proportions. The original design worked, but felt a bit chunky. These would be sleeker, with a more comfortable grip.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/493ac/profiles.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Profiles\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/f058b/profiles.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/c26ae/profiles.png 158w,\n/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/6bdcf/profiles.png 315w,\n/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/f058b/profiles.png 630w,\n/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/40601/profiles.png 945w,\n/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/78612/profiles.png 1260w,\n/static/cb2c56899dae75b0857a64bc7560f05c/493ac/profiles.png 4032w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>I experimented with several different curve profiles, cutting each on the bandsaw and then shaping with rasps and sandpaper. The goal was finding that sweet spot between ergonomic comfort and visual appeal.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/669cd/magnet.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Magnet\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/f058b/magnet.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/c26ae/magnet.png 158w,\n/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/6bdcf/magnet.png 315w,\n/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/f058b/magnet.png 630w,\n/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/40601/magnet.png 945w,\n/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/78612/magnet.png 1260w,\n/static/50a47c4f0167446bd11e8d399c70d40d/669cd/magnet.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The big upgrade for Mark 2: an embedded rare-earth magnet. Always on your fridge and ready to go. A forstner bit created a perfectly sized recess for the magnet.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/493ac/finished.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 75.31645569620254%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Finished\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/f058b/finished.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/c26ae/finished.png 158w,\n/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/6bdcf/finished.png 315w,\n/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/f058b/finished.png 630w,\n/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/40601/finished.png 945w,\n/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/78612/finished.png 1260w,\n/static/4f88fb214aaaaa0a34b197fd6c51c70e/493ac/finished.png 4032w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>The oak grain really pops after a few coats of finish.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 630px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/669cd/collection.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 133.54430379746836%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"Collection\"\n        title=\"\"\n        src=\"/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/f058b/collection.png\"\n        srcset=\"/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/c26ae/collection.png 158w,\n/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/6bdcf/collection.png 315w,\n/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/f058b/collection.png 630w,\n/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/40601/collection.png 945w,\n/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/78612/collection.png 1260w,\n/static/02507ff728e75b667b6722ca5b6eb737/669cd/collection.png 3024w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 630px) 100vw, 630px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>A family of openers emerged from the design process. Each one slightly different as I dialed in the curves. The variations in grain pattern meant no two were exactly alike; a feature, not a bug.</p>\n<p>Iteration is everything in design. The Mark 2 openers were better in every way than the originals, and the lessons learned would carry forward to future projects. Sometimes you have to make something twice to make it right.</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"Pop Tops Mark 2","date":"April 14, 2018","description":null}},"previous":{"fields":{"slug":"/009-paper-towel-holder/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Paper Towel Holder"}},"next":{"fields":{"slug":"/011-shop-upgrade-3/"},"frontmatter":{"title":"Shop Upgrade 3 - Finding the Flow"}}},"pageContext":{"id":"a33034c0-81c8-57cf-9eb7-c5a4df285c0c","previousPostId":"ecc10525-716c-5944-ab62-a7f6de941b66","nextPostId":"d3e91ac3-5068-5494-b614-c893c98ec712"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2841359383"],"slicesMap":{}}